:: HelpMother [childhood]
# Learning Domestic Skills

You try to help your mother with her work, your small hands mimicking her movements. Though your attempts are clumsy, she encourages your efforts.

"That's right," she says as you twist the plant fibers. "Feel how they become stronger when woven together? One fiber alone is weak, but many together can hold great weight."

She shows you how different plants have different properties - some are flexible, others stiff; some absorb water, others repel it. This knowledge has been passed down through generations of women in your tribe.

As you work together, your mother sings a soft working song, the rhythm helping to coordinate your movements. You begin to understand that these tasks are not just chores but a way of connecting to your ancestors and contributing to the tribe's well-being.

